# Every Dockerfile in this context does `COPY src/`, and Python writes
# __pycache__ next to the source the moment anything imports it — including
# the gate's own selftest run locally. Those .pyc files are gitignored, so
# without this they were in the BUILD context but not in the tree: the image
# carried bytes a fresh clone does not have, and the digest a protocol pins
# stopped being a fact about this repository and became a fact about one
# laptop. docker-bake.hcl's first line claims the build is a pure function of
# this tree; this is what makes that true for this context.
# Leading **/ is load-bearing: .dockerignore is NOT gitignore. A bare
# `__pycache__/` matches only a TOP-LEVEL entry, and these live at
# src/__pycache__ and gate/__pycache__, so the bare form silently matched
# nothing and the .pyc files kept shipping.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
